/**
 * @file Data tables for the Map Skins look (`map-skins.js`): the nine realm
 * kits and the tale floor and tale stones of each catalogue map (0-51) and
 * scenario (1-8), keyed by the map's technical name.
 *
 * GENERATED FILE. Do not edit by hand. The maintainers' map-skin converter
 * writes it from their tale skins and the
 * real map catalogue (`src/marl_battlegrounds/modes/team_deathmatch/data`). One hand edit:
 * scenario 5's title reads "Turning the Tide", in the AP heading case that
 * shell.js uses. Plain data and small pure lookups only: no DOM, network, storage or timers. `map-skins.js` reads
 * the floors; `obstacles.js` may read the stones through `map-skins.js`.
 *
 * Tale trees are stored as JSON text per map and parsed on first use, so only
 * the maps a page shows are ever parsed. A tree is a list of nodes
 * `[tag, attributes, mask, children?]`: tag is an export-safe SVG tag (g, path,
 * ellipse, circle, line, rect), attributes hold flat paint only, and mask says
 * in which switch mixes the node shows (-1 = always; otherwise bit i set means
 * it shows in mix i, where mix bit k is the k-th switch of
 * TALE_FLOOR_SWITCHES or TALE_STONE_SWITCHES being on). Coordinates are CSS
 * pixels at TALE_REFERENCE_SCALE pixels per world unit, with (0, 0) at the
 * floor's top-left corner (world x 0, world y = map height).
 *
 * Boundary: a map skin is the same in every view. The tables never hold a
 * champion, a position of one or anything an audience could be denied, so
 * Agent POV and Oracle View read them alike.
 */

/** Pixels per world unit of the stored tale trees. */
export const TALE_REFERENCE_SCALE = 48;

/** Switch ids whose on/off mix picks tale floor nodes (bit k = k-th id on). */
export const TALE_FLOOR_SWITCHES = Object.freeze(["moonlight","floor_grid","spawn_waystones","red_zone_floors","pov_sight_veil"]);

/** Switch ids whose on/off mix picks tale stone nodes (bit k = k-th id on). */
export const TALE_STONE_SWITCHES = Object.freeze(["obstacle_relief","obstacle_shadows","red_zone_floors"]);

/** The most nodes one tale floor or tale stone tree holds (budget bound). */
export const MAX_TALE_NODES = 45;

